.TH MODBUS-CACHE 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-cache \- Modbus TCP caching proxy for single-client devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-cache
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B modbus-cache \-\-dry-run
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B modbus-cache
owns the single Modbus TCP client connection a device allows (Huawei
SUN2000 inverters and their SDongle/EMMA radios accept exactly one) and
multiplexes it: a background loop polls the configured register ranges
into an in-memory cache, any number of clients are served FC3/FC4 reads
from the cache, reads outside the map and other function codes are
forwarded live, and writes (FC05/06/15/16/22/23) are forwarded when
explicitly enabled and audited. A synthesized diagnostics block at
registers 65000\(en65003 lets clients tell cached data from live data.
.PP
Resilience: when the device dies, cached reads keep serving last-known
values and forwarded reads get exception 0x0B; when the device rejects a
range, the poll status is remembered instead of hammering it; garbage from
either side is answered one line at a time and never fatal. Verified
against the fake inverter, fuzzing and stress suites \-\- not against real
hardware.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
config file (ini, \fB[cache]\fR section, snake_case keys). Default:
\fBmodbus_cache.ini\fR next to the script, then the packaged sample; a
missing file is fine. A malformed file is fatal.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
upstream inverter/dongle address. Default \fB127.0.0.1\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
upstream Modbus TCP port. Default \fB5502\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-unit " N"
Modbus unit id (1\(en247). Default \fB1\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " S"
upstream connect/read timeout, seconds. Default \fB3\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " HOST:PORT"
proxy listen address. Default \fB127.0.0.1:15502\fR (loopback only).
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME|PATH"
device profile: a bare name resolved against the shared
\fBprofiles/profiles/\fR directory or a JSON path. Default the bundled
\fBsun2000\fR. Re-read on SIGHUP.
.TP
.BI \-\-selection " all|none|PATH"
which profile entries to fetch: every entry (\fBall\fR, the default), an
empty map (\fBnone\fR \(em every read forwards, nothing is stored), or a
JSON file \fB{"registers": ["pv-power", ...]}\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " S"
seconds between cache polls. Default \fB10\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache-ttl " S"
per-register cache TTL; entries older than this are refetched on the next
read. Default \fB3\(en\fR\fBinterval\fR; \fB0\fR = never expire. Profile
entries may override per entry (\fBttl\fR field).
.TP
.BI \-\-read-delay " S"
seconds between consecutive device reads within a poll cycle. Default
\fB0.05\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-merge-gap " N"
maximum register gap when merging ranges into block reads (\fB0\fR = read
separately). Default \fB8\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-write
forward write requests to the device. Off by default (they are refused
with a Modbus illegal-function exception).
.TP
.BI \-\-write-registers " RANGES"
register ranges a forwarded write may touch: comma-separated
\fBSTART:COUNT\fR (e.g. \fB47400:100,47600:100\fR). Default \fBany\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-connect-acl " LIST"
clients allowed to connect: \fBany\fR (the default) or comma-separated
IPs/CIDR prefixes, IPv4 or IPv6.
.TP
.BI \-\-write-acl " LIST"
clients allowed to write; still requires \fB--allow-write\fR. Default
\fBany\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-control-port " TARGET"
the JSON-lines control server: a unix socket path or a TCP port (bound to
127.0.0.1). Default \fB/tmp/modbus-cache-\fR\fI<listen-port>\fB.socket\fR;
\fB0\fR = off.
.TP
.BI \-\-control-token " TOKEN"
require a token on TCP control connections (the first command must be
\fB{"cmd": "auth", "token": "..."}\fR). The unix socket needs no token.
.TP
.BI \-\-control-token-file " FILE"
the token from a file (the first line; a systemd \fBLoadCredential\fR) \(em
instead of \fB--control-token\fR; giving both is an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-reads-audit " S"
audit one READS tally per client per this many seconds (default
\fB300\fR); \fB0\fR = off.
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics-port " N"
serve the cache's own Prometheus \fB/metrics\fR on 127.0.0.1:\fIN\fR (the
\fBmodbus_cache_*\fR gauges). Off by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics-token " TOKEN"
require \fBAuthorization: Bearer\fR on the metrics endpoint.
.TP
.BI \-\-metrics-token-file " FILE"
the metrics bearer token from a file (the first line); mutually exclusive
with \fB--metrics-token\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit-log " FILE|\-"
the append-only audit trail. Default the XDG state home
(\fB~/.local/state/modbus-cache/audit.log\fR); \fB\-\fR = stdout (docker
logs / journald); the trail falls back to stdout when the file is
unwritable.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit-max-mb " N"
rotate the audit trail at this size (default \fB10\fR); \fB0\fR =
unbounded.
.TP
.B \-\-audit-daily
also rotate the audit trail at UTC midnight.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep. Default \fB3\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no-audit-log
disable the audit trail.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-clients " N"
refuse further connections past this many simultaneous clients (default
\fB64\fR; \fB0\fR = unlimited).
.TP
.BI \-\-client-timeout " S"
disconnect clients silent for this many seconds (default \fB300\fR;
\fB0\fR = never).
.TP
.BI \-\-log-level " LEVEL"
\fBDEBUG\fR adds per-client traffic and per-poll detail. Default
\fBINFO\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-log-access
log client connects/disconnects at INFO instead of DEBUG.
.TP
.B \-\-local-time
log timestamps in the system time zone instead of UTC.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
validate the configuration and the register map, print the effective
settings and exit without binding or contacting anything.
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
reload the configuration and the register map without dropping clients
(the file always wins over live settings; a broken file keeps the previous
state). The listen address and the log level need a restart.
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
clean the cache: all cached values, on-demand entries and poll-status
errors are dropped; the poller repopulates immediately.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
graceful shutdown.
.SH CONTROL
The control server speaks JSON lines: one request
\fB{"cmd": "..."}\fR per line, one reply
\fB{"status": "ok|err|bye", "text": "..."}\fR per line. Commands
(the settings registry drives the grammar):
.BR set ", " unset ", " show ", " help ,
the reports
.BR inspect ", " "show status" ", " "show connections" ", " "show cache" " [all]" ", " "show version" ,
the ops
.BR clear\ cache ", " restart ", " shutdown ", " quit .
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B set <setting> <value>
changes a setting live (interval, ttl, read-delay, merge-gap,
allow-write, write-registers, max-clients, client-timeout, reads-audit,
log-level, profile, selection, connect-acl, write-acl, timeout); a
SIGHUP re-applies the config (the file always wins).
.IP \(bu 2
.B show cache all
prints every cached entry: name, words, age, expiry, poll status.
.IP \(bu 2
.B clear cache
/ SIGUSR1, \fBrestart\fR (drop the upstream + the cache, repoll),
\fBshutdown\fR (the same as SIGTERM).
.RE
.PP
See
.BR modbus-cache-ctl (1)
and
.BR modbus-cache-cli (1)
for the clients.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MODBUS_CACHE_CTL
default control target for the daemon's clients (flag \fB--control-port\fR
wins).
.TP
.B MODBUS_CACHE_*
every flag has an environment twin (\fBMODBUS_CACHE_HOST\fR,
\fBMODBUS_CACHE_LISTEN\fR, \fBMODBUS_CACHE_ALLOW_WRITE\fR, ...); the flag
wins over the env, the env over the ini.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/modbus-cache-<port>.socket
the default control socket (stale files replaced, unlinked on shutdown).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/modbus-cache/audit.log
the default audit trail.
.TP
.I cache/modbus_cache.ini ", " cache/selection.json
the packaged sample config and the example selection.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success (\fB--dry-run\fR: valid configuration).
.TP
.B 1
invalid configuration (reason on stderr; \fB--dry-run\fR only).
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-cache-ctl (1),
.BR modbus-cache-cli (1),
.BR modbus-scraper (1),
.BR modbus-fake-inverter (1)
.PP
\fBcache/README.md\fR in the suite checkout \(em the full documentation.
